From: buntOS contributors
Subject: [PATCH] power: supply: mt6375-charger: do not end a charge far under the voltage limit

The chip ends a charge on a current under IEOC anywhere above where
charging comes back. That is CV - VREC, 4.14 V here, or about 73 % on
this battery. It does not wait for the voltage limit. The low current as
a source comes up is enough. The chip then goes through EOC and
background charging to DONE, which reads as Full, and the source carries
the system with nothing going into the battery. The voltage then has no
reason to fall under 4.14 V.

On the device this came 9 seconds after a hard reset, at 4.16 V and 73
%, with the battery current at 0 from then on. EOC_RST, which the
MediaTek driver has as reset_eoc_state, brought it back at once to +1.86
A from a 9 V 2 A contract.

A charge that really ended did so at the voltage limit. Reset the state
when the battery is more than 100 mV under that, at the next look of
this driver. That is also the vrec of the MediaTek driver, so a battery
that really was full can come back there rather than at 200 mV down.

At a real full charge the chip ended at 4.335 V and +0.34 A, and it
stayed in DONE for the 15 minutes watched.

---
 drivers/power/supply/mt6375-charger.c | 23 +++++++++++++++++++++--
 1 file changed, 21 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)

diff --git a/drivers/power/supply/mt6375-charger.c b/drivers/power/supply/mt6375-charger.c
index c1347b6..31e36fb 100644
--- a/drivers/power/supply/mt6375-charger.c
+++ b/drivers/power/supply/mt6375-charger.c
@@ -136,6 +136,8 @@
 /* vrec: how far under the voltage limit charging comes back */
 #define MT6375_CHG_VREC_UV		200000
 #define MT6375_CHG_VREC_200MV		1
+/* A charge ending further than this under the voltage limit did not end */
+#define MT6375_CHG_EOC_MARGIN_UV	100000
 /* chg-tmr, chg-tmr-en: 5 hours from 0 in steps of 5 hours */
 #define MT6375_CHG_TMR_10H		1
 /* The stock charger thread looks every 10 seconds */
@@ -152,8 +154,8 @@
 
 enum mt6375_chg_field {
 	F_CHG_EN, F_BUCK_EN, F_HZ, F_IAICR, F_ILIM_EN, F_VMIVR, F_CV, F_VREC,
-	F_CC, F_CHG_TMR, F_CHG_TMR_EN, F_TE, F_IEOC, F_BLEED_DIS_EN, F_WDT_EN,
-	F_IC_STAT, F_ST_PWR_RDY, F_MAX,
+	F_CC, F_CHG_TMR, F_CHG_TMR_EN, F_EOC_RST, F_TE, F_IEOC, F_BLEED_DIS_EN,
+	F_WDT_EN, F_IC_STAT, F_ST_PWR_RDY, F_MAX,
 };
 
 static const struct reg_field mt6375_chg_reg_fields[F_MAX] = {
@@ -168,6 +170,7 @@ static const struct reg_field mt6375_chg_reg_fields[F_MAX] = {
 	[F_CC] = REG_FIELD(MT6375_REG_CHG_ICHG, 0, 5),
 	[F_CHG_TMR] = REG_FIELD(MT6375_REG_CHG_TMR, 4, 5),
 	[F_CHG_TMR_EN] = REG_FIELD(MT6375_REG_CHG_TMR, 7, 7),
+	[F_EOC_RST] = REG_FIELD(MT6375_REG_CHG_EOC, 0, 0),
 	[F_TE] = REG_FIELD(MT6375_REG_CHG_EOC, 1, 1),
 	[F_IEOC] = REG_FIELD(MT6375_REG_CHG_EOC, 4, 7),
 	[F_BLEED_DIS_EN] = REG_FIELD(MT6375_REG_CHG_VSYS, 7, 7),
@@ -1382,6 +1385,22 @@ static void mt6375_chg_control(struct mt6375_chg *chg,
 		ret = regmap_field_write(chg->fields[F_CHG_EN], 1);
 		if (ret)
 			goto stop;
+
+		/*
+		 * The chip ends a charge on a low current alone, anywhere above
+		 * where charging comes back. The current as a source comes up
+		 * does that, at 73 % here, and it then stays "full" with the
+		 * source carrying the system. A charge that ended for real did
+		 * so at the voltage limit.
+		 */
+		if (!now->err && now->vbat_uv < cv - MT6375_CHG_EOC_MARGIN_UV &&
+		    (stat == MT6375_CHG_STAT_EOC ||
+		     stat == MT6375_CHG_STAT_BKGND ||
+		     stat == MT6375_CHG_STAT_DONE)) {
+			ret = regmap_field_write(chg->fields[F_EOC_RST], 1);
+			if (ret)
+				goto stop;
+		}
 	}
 
 	ret = stop_ret;
